+# HIL Sign‑off Workflow
+
+This document describes the automated + human steps required for HIL sign‑off before promoting models to field devices.
+
+1) Prepare HIL scenario
+ - Define scenario id and associated test script that exercises the system and produces logs.
+ - Ensure HIL harness captures telemetry, video and logs and stores them to artifact location (S3/LakeFS).
+
+2) Schedule HIL job
+ - Use k8s/hil/hil-signoff-job.yaml to run the HIL scenario in the lab cluster (or run hil/hil_runner.py locally/in CI).
+ - The job writes a JSON result artifact and stores logs in configured artifact store.
+
+3) Produce evidence pack
+ - Evidence pack must include:
+   - scenario id, run id, test script, input data, telemetry, logs, signed artifacts (.sig), and any analysis reports.
+   - signatures: cosign-signed artifact + Rekor entry.
+
+4) Encrypt and store originals
+ - If evidence contains PII or raw sensor data, run scripts/encrypt_and_store_original.sh to encrypt originals and upload to restricted bucket.
+ - Store pointer to encrypted original in MCP evidence record.
+
+5) Create A2A approval request
+ - Submit an A2A approval request referencing evidence pack (use approver service).
+ - The approver must be a qualified engineer/authority and must sign the approval record (approver service will KMS-sign approval).
+
+6) Audit & retention
+ - Approved evidence packs are stored in MCP and archived per retention policy.
+ - Rejected evidence triggers remediation and retest.
+
+7) Promotion
+ - Only after A2A approval and signed evidence should the model be promoted to OTA rollouts.
+
+Notes:
+ - Maintain traceability: link FMEA entries to each HIL run and evidence pack.
+ - Keep a register of approvers and their qualification records alongside approvals.
+
